bhyve-viewer presents a bhyve guest's GPU output in a window on the host's
Wayland compositor, with no copy and no video encoding in the path.

A guest using virtio-gpu with venus renders on the host GPU, so its images
are already in host memory.  Running a compositor and VNC server inside the
guest ships that framebuffer into the guest purely so the guest can capture
and encode it back out, which costs guest CPU and adds latency for nothing.
Instead bhyve exports the scanout as a dma_buf and hands the descriptor to
this program over a unix socket.

Requires a bhyve built with BHYVE_VIRGL_SUPPORT and a virtio-gpu device
configured with display=unix:/path/to/socket, and a host compositor that
offers zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1.
